{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (rebar-debug, Phase 1 complete) — DISPOSITION: ESCALATE (design decision required; not auto-landed)\n\nSTEP 0 / ORIENT\n- 0(a) tracker sweep: no duplicate. This ticket is the single tracker for the deferred run_sweep site. Sibling injurious-pugnacious-azurevase (c0f6, in_progress) covers a DIFFERENT set (str()/realpath()/abspath() variants), not this site.\n- 0(b) reported-against floor: filed as a split-off from auspicial-friended-merganser (2ec7, Gerrit 2326, 98f21fbc). Suspect path src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py unchanged on origin/main since (verified).\n- 0(c) worktree at origin/main 82a0d5cd328f (= origin/main).\n\nPROVEN ROOT CAUSE (dynamic, runtime-confirmed)\nrun_sweep(tracker) at src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:222 hardcodes repo_root = os.path.dirname(tracker) and passes it EXPLICITLY to compact.compact_all_cli([], repo_root=repo_root). compact_all_cli reads the [compact] config via config.compose_config(repo_root).compact (threshold, COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS). On a RELOCATED store (REBAR_TRACKER_DIR outside the checkout — the deployed MCP topology: store at /var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets, code at /app) the store's parent has no rebar.toml, so the sweep reads DEFAULT compaction config (threshold=10, horizon=1800s) instead of the code-root config. tracker_dir stays correct (REBAR_TRACKER_DIR wins verbatim), so the sweep folds the RIGHT tickets by the WRONG rule. Impact is milder than the parent's gate-disable: no gate is silently turned off; a non-default [compact] config is ignored.\n\nPROOF (discriminating experiment, runtime)\nRelocated store (REBAR_TRACKER_DIR outside checkout), code-root rebar.toml sets [compact] threshold=1, COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS=0. Seeded a fresh 4-comment task.\n- run_sweep(tracker): SNAPSHOT NOT written — read default threshold/horizon from dirname(tracker), folded nothing (RED).\n- On the SAME store, compact_all_cli([], repo_root=<code root>) DID fold (SNAPSHOT written).\nOnly variable = repo_root (dirname(tracker) vs code root). Confirms repo_root resolution is the sole cause; rules out \"events not foldable\" / \"store misresolved\".\n\nDEFECT LEGITIMACY: defect. The relocatable store is a SUPPORTED feature (EV-3b; tracker_dir_override; scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py). Same construct class as auspicial-friended-merganser (closed Fixed) and chuffy-arbored-goldfish (closed Fixed). This site is the ONE the AC#4 guard explicitly sanctions/defers.\n\nDEFECT ORIGIN (caused_by): the run_sweep dirname(tracker) line was introduced by commit d2dea317ec94 (\"Trigger compaction from the close, out of band\"), rebar-ticket 1fde-becd-942a-4351 (gaudy-gangrenous-basilisk). git blame -L222,222 is unambiguous and non-carrier (that commit WROTE the line); the site was born wrong (never handled a relocated store), so class = plan_defect. NOTE / divergence from the whole-class default: the parent auspicial attributed to 65e3-1fc6-5f3b-4c67 (stab-bunch-foyer), which introduced the transition.py gate site — a DIFFERENT commit. Each site of the shared construct class was shipped by its own commit; this site's is 1fde. caused_by link recorded (6bf1 -> 1fde).\n\nWHY ESCALATE (the deferred design decision is real, not stale)\nAC#1 requires the detached-child path to receive a correct code root, and AC#3 requires ZERO sanctioned sites — so the sync path alone cannot close this. The blocker is genuine and specific: WHAT durable code root should the detached child receive?\n- maybe_compact already HAS a resolved repo_root (transition_close: str(config.repo_root(repo_root))), and spawn_detached already supports threading extra argv strings (its docstring documents the optional-sentinel pattern) — so the mechanical plumbing exists.\n- BUT the two supported topologies want DIFFERENT sources:\n  * Deployment (truly relocated store, STABLE /app via REBAR_ROOT): the child should get maybe_compact's repo_root (=/app). Correct and durable.\n  * Local `make worktree` (store co-located via a .tickets-tracker SYMLINK; EPHEMERAL worktree code root): transition_close's repo_root = git-toplevel-of-cwd = the ephemeral worktree, which dies with the worktree. Today _spawn_detached_sweep deliberately hands the child StorePaths(tracker).canonical, and dirname(canonical) = the DURABLE main checkout — which is CORRECT locally. Naively threading maybe_compact's repo_root would point the outliving child at a dying worktree (a re-run of the durability class of bugs 3198/93a9), degrading to default config after teardown.\nThere is no existing helper returning the right durable code root for BOTH topologies; reconciling them (argv vs env; spawning-repo-root vs canonical-store-parent; how to stay durable across worktree teardown) is a config-root-discovery / process-detachment SEMANTICS decision. That exceeds the behavior-preserving/localized bar auspicial's other 8 sites met, exactly as this ticket's description anticipated.\n\nRECOMMENDED DISPOSITION\nTreat as a small design ticket, not a mechanical mirror. Recommended design: give run_sweep an optional second argv param (spawn_detached sentinel \"\"), and have maybe_compact pass a DURABILITY-RESOLVED code root — REBAR_ROOT/explicit when set (covers the deployment), else fall back to dirname(StorePaths(tracker).canonical) (covers the local co-located-symlink worktree, preserving today's correct behavior). run_sweep threads it into compact_all_cli; then remove the # repo-root-ok: sanction (AC#3 -> zero allowlisted sites) and add the guard-clean assertion. RED->GREEN oracle: (1) the relocated-store fold proven RED above (sync path), (2) a _spawn_detached_sweep argv-threading unit assertion (mirrors test_a_detached_sweep_child_is_handed_the_canonical_store_tracker) for the detached path. This needs a human design sign-off on the durable-root resolution rule before implementation; per agent policy I am not landing it unilaterally.\n\nSCOPE/CALLERS: run_sweep has exactly two callers — maybe_compact (sync trigger=always) and the detached child entry via spawn_detached (string ref). Blast radius is contained to compact_trigger.py + the spawn argv contract. No new dependency, no new capability."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787948361662822001,"uuid":"25af228c-653a-4d47-9c02-2aecbe3ae187"}